  "created": "2022-11-09T00:00:00Z",
  "added": "2022-03-01T00:00:00Z",
  "contentCreated": "2008-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "origin": "Code collected from the public GitHub-on-BigQuery dataset, using the same programming-language selection as AlphaCode. Deduplicated on exact matches and filtered for source files with 100-200,000 characters, 15-65% alphabetic characters, max line length 20-1000 characters, and token-length standard deviation > 3. Due to a bug in the pre-processing pipeline, the dataset was filtered for GPL licenses only — this is documented in the ROOTS paper (Section 2.1, 'GitHub Code') as an unintended restriction. The license field carries the GPL-3.0 IRI as the representative license of the files that survived the buggy filter; the underlying GitHub repositories actually carry a mix of GPL-family licenses (GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, AGPL, LGPL) — this is both the per-document multi-license aggregate problem (Gap B) and a distinct data-quality/provenance-honesty case: a dataset whose license field reflects a processing artifact rather than the intended selection. See notes/stress-test-bloom-roots.md (Gap F discussion). ROOTS was released as a gated subset subject to the BigScience ethical charter.",
